# Cursor Rules — Starter Journey

Read CLAUDE.md at the repo root for full project context. This file adds Cursor-specific guidance.

## Quick start

The Docusaurus project is at `docs/starter-journey/` (not the repo root). To start the dev server:

```bash
cd docs/starter-journey && npm install && npm run start -- --port 3000
```

## Before editing documentation

1. Read `docs/STYLE.md` for the two page templates (Technical and Educational) and writing rules.
2. Check `docs/starter-journey/sidebars.ts` to understand the current section numbering and structure.
3. After any doc or sidebar change, run `npm run build` from `docs/starter-journey/` to catch broken links.

## File patterns

- **Doc pages:** `docs/starter-journey/docs/**/*.md` — use markdown, not MDX, unless you need React imports.
- **Sidebar config:** `docs/starter-journey/sidebars.ts` — manually managed. Every new page must be registered here.
- **Site config:** `docs/starter-journey/docusaurus.config.ts` — plugins, navbar, footer, gtag.
- **Images:** `docs/starter-journey/static/img/` — prefix with section slug (e.g., `infra-*.png`).
- **Blog posts:** `docs/starter-journey/blog/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.mdx`.

## Rules for generated content

- Only use `:::tip`, `:::warning`, `:::danger` admonitions. No `:::info`, `:::success`, `:::note`.
- Every page needs the shared top chrome (frontmatter + value prop + prereqs) and bottom chrome (`## Next` with Do next / Learn why / Reference).
- Internal links use `/docs/<path>` format. Never use relative file paths.
- No filler phrases. See the banned-phrases list in `docs/STYLE.md`.
- One idea per sentence. Paragraphs under 4 sentences. Active voice.

## Git workflow

- Create feature branches from `main` for all changes.
- PRs to `main` run a build check via GitHub Actions (`test-deploy.yml`).
- Merges to `main` auto-deploy to GitHub Pages (`deploy.yml`).
- Weekly section freshness runs via `section-freshness.yml`; bump `docs/starter-journey/section-freshness.csv` when you update a journey section.
- Do not commit `node_modules/`, `build/`, or `.docusaurus/`.
